From: atty303 <atty303@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mfreadwrite: drain Source Reader transforms on demand

Keep a stream in an explicit draining state after the media source reaches
EOS. Send MFT_MESSAGE_COMMAND_DRAIN once per transform, but service the chain
only while a Source Reader request is pending. If downstream backpressure
outlives that request, retain the unsubmitted sample and resume it from the
next ReadSample call. Publish EOS only after the final transform reports that
it needs more input or has reached end of stream.

This preserves normal Source Reader backpressure for video and other media
while allowing split decoder output, including the final WMA frame, to be
returned over subsequent ReadSample calls instead of being discarded behind
EOS. Continue servicing selected streams after MEEndOfPresentation until each
stream has completed its transform drain. Return drain failures as Source
Reader errors with the original HRESULT.
---
 dlls/mfreadwrite/reader.c | 305 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 247 insertions(+), 58 deletions(-)

